{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings","id":553801,"title":"My issues with the new direction with Seemings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-13T21:16:16-07:00","id":553801,"title":"My issues with the new direction with Seemings","content":"Now that I've had time to distill my thoughts around this new direction for Seeming. I'd like to speak my opinion.<br /> <br /> At first I was super excited for the change. As a base idea I think it works better than 1e. Though, I may not be following the reasoning behind the new Seeming direction. What I understand is that the intention is for Seeming to speak of the Soul powered exertion to rewrite the narrative being crafted from the Story that is the True Fae/Keeper.<br /> <br /> Johnny Appleseed does a thing and redefines himself and his reality to shake off the narrative structure he was bound within. He is escaping the Fairy Tale by writing the next page with his soul.<br /> Seeming therefore are Archetypes Lost fall into during that process. Beasts rewrote the sotry by going National Geographic. Darklings rewrote the story by doing what ever it took. Fairest rewrote the story by waking others up to the limitations being placed upon them. But taking the pen in hand is an action of Fairy. Doing so without having the limitless Identity of the Gentry comes at the cost of being swept up into this new narrative. This story of escape. The Lost quickly loses control and find their choice not only defines their journey home but also redefines their own identity.<br /> <br /> That is what I reason was the idea behind this new concept. Your Seeming is a symbol of the story of your escape.<br /> <br /> I've considered the few samples put out for discussion and I do not think these write ups do justice to the concept at hand. The largest issue is that they limit conceptual ideas into very narrow Archetypes. If the Archetype were broader or written more loosely I feel they would serve my players and myself better when making changelings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:31:23-07:00","id":554143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalvin8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings#post553801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've considered the few samples put out for discussion and I do not think these write ups do justice to the concept at hand. The largest issue is that they limit conceptual ideas into very narrow Archetypes. If the Archetype were broader or written more loosely I feel they would serve my players and myself better when making changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my issue with it as well; which I discussed at length, at very very long length, when they first came out.<br /> <br /> My suggestion was to just rename the section entitled &quot;Background&quot; to &quot;Sample charachter&quot;. Move the first part of &quot;The Escape&quot; to the end of &quot;Sample Character&quot;. Then move the Sample Character section to the end of the write up.<br /> <br /> Given that MachiveIV has already said he won't ask for significant rewrites I think that's the best that can be done. (Besides, it is a good sample charachter, I just wish it wasn't the only one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-14-2015, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:35:20-07:00","id":554567,"title":"","content":"I agree with and would support King's Raven's solution, which is funny, because I was one of Raven's most vocal opponents in the very long discussion that eventually lead to that conclusion. I think that would go a long way towards making it more clear that the apparently narrow character concept is meant as merely one example of a much broader archetype. I'm pretty sure it was always meant to be an example, rather than a blueprint all characters of the Seeming follow. But evidently that did not come across clearly to a lot of people, and I think Raven's proposal does a good job of making that more clear, without sacrificing what are in my opinion very powerfully written example characters.<br /> <br /> All of that said, we can't and shouldn't expect the writers to follow the suggestions of a specific fan's proposal to the letter. I think what ever changes they do make (and David H. has said he wants to make the potential conceptual breadth of the Seemmgs more obvious in the final version) will address these concerns, as long as we keep in mind that these are examples meant to inspire our own characters, not rules meant to restrict our creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-14-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:31:03-07:00","id":554938,"title":"","content":"I totally missed that these samples were example characters. I understood them to be fragments of the rough Seeming themselves.<br /> <br /> Looking back at the posts. David never suggested that these were examples created from another source. So I'm confused.<br /> <br /> Is the intention to use the (Bone/Blood from Wolf) archetypes and label them Curse and Blessing? Those Archtype(Virtue/Vice) were tied in with willpower. Perhaps if I read this discussion you guys had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:45:12-07:00","id":554943,"title":"","content":"No, the drafts were of the writeups for the Seemings. It's just that obviously not every Darkling needs to have been an extremely loyal person before being taken and have betrayed someone to escape. Or, at least, I thought that was obvious and apparently not everyone agreed. It's my understanding that the &quot;background&quot; section and the &quot;escape&quot; section were written to show one way a character might follow the more general Darkling trend of &quot;did what had to be done to escape.&quot; Same for the other Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:38:33-07:00","id":555043,"title":"","content":"Yeah, more (shorter) examples would perhaps have been more evocative but at the very least presenting the writeups as an example of the seeming would help avoid the seemings being narrowly stereotyped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:17:15-07:00","id":555269,"title":"","content":"I just noticed that there is a new Seventh Seeming being planned. I hadn't thought is possible to expound on the Seeming Archetypes. But now that Seeming is your soul's response to your escape, I can see new ground to expound on Seeming. Is there some kind for framing for these? Are we drawing on psychological theory of survivors or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:53:01-07:00","id":555283,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly just adding the new direction for Seemings to the list of reasons why I'm really not excited for 2e. The game as a whole appears to be headed in a direction that I really don't care for, and has lost the magic of the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:04:31-07:00","id":555287,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the method of escape giving you the Seeming, but in that case tying them to physical appearances seems odd to me. <br /> <br /> I also really do not like the new direction of the Fairest, which were my favorite 1E splat because of their fey callousness, whereas now their whole thing is feeling responsibility more than anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6465-eleusis","name":"Eleusis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:48:20-07:00","id":555325,"title":"","content":"I agree. My own Fairest is calloused and cold. His escape had nothing to do with any kind of sense of personal responsibility. I'm open to re-contextualizing the character. But I want it to be on my terms. Not in adherence to push a Seeming into defacto leadership.<br /> <br /> Are all Fairest Seeming born from a latent responsibility to lead others to undiscovered greatness? Because that is nearly an opposite of most of the 1e Fairest thematic. That is more a Kith (Muse) from 1e than a proper cohesion to a choice. It seems Instead most 1e Fairest would become Darklings. For me, this is a welcome novelty, so long as the Seeming are broad enough give space to stubborn players to keep their cake as they eat it too. Old Players of the first edition are the first audience biting at the bit for a new edition. For most of my players, these samples have soured them to the idea of new setting. I can get them excited for the new paradigm of Seeming is how you escaped. But after reading the samples, they came back to confused.<br /> <br /> I too, as I stated above; love the new context for Seeming. The Physical adherence therein is a thematic of the Setting. Arcadia is a story, and when mortals are forced into it's prose they find themselves almost as mutable as the Gentry around them. It makes sense that Seeming is the reflection of your character's choice to escape. And imprinting made about by the will of your soul to get free.<br /> My issue is with the seemingly narrow categorization of those choices and their circumstances.<br /> <br /> It seems this conversation was had. I just wish I saw David's response. How broad is broad? This change to Seeming has affected the entire setting. Old Players will be first interested in porting over their old characters. For most others who I know, these changes are crippling. They are fraught over how their character has lost their Seeming altogether based on the durance they wrote for their character years ago. Character they have played in many campaigns ever since.<br /> <br /> I have one friend who plays a Trickster Fox Changeling. A Beast seeming. For this player the novelty of the character includes the thematic of the Beast Seeming, which for her has been the largest descriptor of her character for three years now.<br /> The Character is highly social, as befitting a sly trickster and suave manipulator. But 2e Beast overtly contextualizes the seeming as anti-social, even anti-culture. She is presently frustrated with how to re-frame her own character to this new design. The Cruse and Blessing mechanics directly conflict with the character's design. I should further state she is very open to changing this character's Seeming. But for her the new Beast design/sample/example rubs her raw.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest here. If I can't get the players that sit at my table excited about 2e Changeling. I have no use for it. This thread is my attempt to make my concerns known. I hope it is coming across respectfully. I love a lot of the rest that is coming with this new edition of Changeling. But for five out of seven of my friends, these samples alone have turned them cold to even broaching the topic of a 2e game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:00:22-07:00","id":555329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalvin8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555325#post555325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. My own Fairest is calloused and cold. His escape had nothing to do with any kind of sense of personal responsibility. I'm open to re-contextualizing the character. But I want it to be on my terms. Not in adherence to push a Seeming into defacto leadership.<br /> <br /> Are all Fairest Seeming born from a latent responsibility to lead others to undiscovered greatness? Because that is nearly an opposite of most of the 1e Fairest thematic. That is more a Kith (Muse) from 1e than a proper cohesion to a choice. It seems Instead most 1e Fairest would become Darklings. For me, this is a welcome novelty, so long as the Seeming are broad enough give space to stubborn players to keep their cake as they eat it too. Old Players of the first edition are the first audience biting at the bit for a new edition. For most of my players, these samples have soured them to the idea of new setting. I can get them excited for the new paradigm of Seeming is how you escaped. But after reading the samples, they came back to confused.<br /> <br /> I too, as I stated above; love the new context for Seeming. The Physical adherence therein is a thematic of the Setting. Arcadia is a story, and when mortals are forced into it's prose they find themselves almost as mutable as the Gentry around them. It makes sense that Seeming is the reflection of your character's choice to escape. And imprinting made about by the will of your soul to get free.<br /> My issue is with the seemingly narrow categorization of those choices and their circumstances.<br /> <br /> It seems this conversation was had. I just wish I saw David's response. How broad is broad? This change to Seeming has affected the entire setting. Old Players will be first interested in porting over their old characters. For most others who I know, these changes are crippling. They are fraught over how their character has lost their Seeming altogether based on the durance they wrote for their character years ago. Character they have played in many campaigns ever since.<br /> <br /> I have one friend who plays a Trickster Fox Changeling. A Beast seeming. For this player the novelty of the character includes the thematic of the Beast Seeming, which for her has been the largest descriptor of her character for three years now.<br /> The Character is highly social, as befitting a sly trickster and suave manipulator. But 2e Beast overtly contextualizes the seeming as anti-social, even anti-culture. She is presently frustrated with how to re-frame her own character to this new design. The Cruse and Blessing mechanics directly conflict with the character's design. I should further state she is very open to changing this character's Seeming. But for her the new Beast design/sample/example rubs her raw.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest here. If I can't get the players that sit at my table excited about 2e Changeling. I have no use for it. This thread is my attempt to make my concerns known. I hope it is coming across respectfully. I love a lot of the rest that is coming with this new edition of Changeling. But for five out of seven of my friends, these samples alone have turned them cold to even broaching the topic of a 2e game.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what was Seeming seems like it will now be Kith.<br /> <br /> The cruel, aloof, beautiful Ice Queen (personality, not powers) that used to be straight kithless Fairest might now be a Pretty-person Kith Darkling or Elemental.<br /> <br /> The Trickster Fox is probably the Trickster Kith... and might still be a Beast, Beasts break social norms and refuse to be contained, pranks and trickery fulfill that. But they could instead be a Wizened or Fairest Trickster and keep the Fox Mein.<br /> <br /> Also: fraught with what? Worry? Revulsion? Anxiety? Giddyness? Wariness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-15-2015, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:11:10-07:00","id":555333,"title":"","content":"You are in general voicing my opinion Khalvin8, so I'm afraid I can't add that much to the discussion other than that you are not alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:25:52-07:00","id":555357,"title":"","content":"Anxiety and confusion. Some anger about the change being a change at all. But I was able to talk up the opportunities the change opens up. All of these conversations were rather adult. She gets that the new place of Kiths is just to assume the old space of Seeming. She understands that even in 1e those kiths made up the bulk mechanical tools the character was most apt to take advantage of. It seems to come down to language for her and myself really.<br /> <br /> Seeming was what your character was. Kith was just segmentation of that Seeming. Things have changed and arguably for the better.<br /> For both of us, or I should say six of us; It comes to the categories being presented through Seemings. The choices and context of those choices in these samples.<br /> Just keeping the three thus far. What Seeming is your character if they escaped with their Social Humanity intact, Their Personal Morality intact, and didn't escape with a cohort of other Lost souls? They wouldn\u2019t be a Beast, a Darkling, Or a Fairest. And thus I'm at a lost with my own character. He escaped with his pride as a human, his relative morality secured, and alone. That limits from his old Seeming and two others.<br /> Considering the pattern. It makes him most likely a wizened. In fact nearly all of my players would end up playing Wizened if they kept their old Characters.<br /> I'm assuming the Wizened escape method has something to with hard effort and practiced skill. That seems to catch nearly all of the old Characters made in 1e. And really because most 1e Lost escaped alone. (So not a Fairest) and did so without choosing to do something blatantly villainous (not a Darkling)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:30:23-07:00","id":555632,"title":"","content":"My friend was interested in Changeling.<br /> <br /> Now he is not.<br /> <br /> His reason? He <i>has</i> to pick a Kith... out of a list of about 100.<br /> <br /> He <i>hates</i> having to pick one option off a long list - at least in 1e he had the choice of not picking a Kith, and the Kiths were in lists of about 20.<br /> <br /> That's my issue with the shift in focus; Kiths are so much more important now, so you can't really avoid interacting with THE LIST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:24:41-07:00","id":555870,"title":"","content":"You could artificially shorten the list for him. Ask him what what he want his character to be good at. Then find five Kiths that mechanically support that. I'd be happy to do that leg work. The Kith samples are not very long.<br /> He doesn't have to dig through the list. If he is still reluctant to play even after you remove the list as a barrier then I don't think it is a list that is turning him off from the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:32:27-07:00","id":555873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555632#post555632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His reason? He <i>has</i> to pick a Kith... out of a list of about 100.<br /> <br /> He <i>hates</i> having to pick one option off a long list - at least in 1e he had the choice of not picking a Kith, and the Kiths were in lists of about 20.<br /> <br /> That's my issue with the shift in focus; Kiths are so much more important now, so you can't really avoid interacting with THE LIST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not ask him to describe his charachters &quot;faerie tale role&quot; in one sentence: &quot;cindarella&quot;, &quot;knight in shining armour&quot; - and pick a kith for him?<br /> <br /> edit - I realise that is working around the issue but the Kith list isn't going to go away (and I like it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-15-2015, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T12:02:11-07:00","id":555897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555873#post555873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit - I realise that is working around the issue but the Kith list isn't going to go away (and I like it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Question is if it really be <b>A List</b> in 2ED corebook? Like quick sum up of all Kiths on one page to look at and full desctiption on few others. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:47:50-07:00","id":556357,"title":"","content":"I would rather have had one's escape be reflected in particular unique fae powers or merits than the way Seeming is going for the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:31:45-07:00","id":556502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555873#post555873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not ask him to describe his charachters &quot;faerie tale role&quot; in one sentence: &quot;cindarella&quot;, &quot;knight in shining armour&quot; - and pick a kith for him?<br /> <br /> edit - I realise that is working around the issue but the Kith list isn't going to go away (and I like it)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a part of that is just that huge lists are completely incomprehensible for some people. For all the unnecessary duplication in 1E Kiths, at the very least it whittled down the hundred-ish Kiths down to about a dozen or less for any individual character once you selected a seeming. It's one of the problems with Embeds in Demon as well: The possibility space is freaking enormous and lots of people get decision paralysis. I worry that the free contracts will have the same issue: While I didn't necessarily agree with the devs on the free-flowing vs tiered structure contract thing, it does make it more comprehensible at one end.<br /> <br /> Rough groupings of about a dozen kiths would probably do a LOT to make it more manageable - bite sized chunks all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:12:38-07:00","id":556589,"title":"","content":"Grouping the Kiths into larger families is best way to go. But how do you classify them? By thematic fluff or by mechanical role?<br /> <br /> As for Seeming Blessing and Curse, vs Merits/Fae Entitlements. I don't see how these are mutually exclusive. I imagine there will be Merits as well as Affinity Contractsdefined by Seeming. The samples are just that. We don;t know what more will be exclusive to Seemings. Just the overarching themes they are writing for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:59:22-07:00","id":557183,"title":"","content":"Decision paralysis in 1e wasn't really that great even with Kiths by Seeming, because there were overlapping Kiths and Dual Kith that completely muddied the water.<br /> <br /> I think that if you have a decent idea in your head about what happened in your character's Durance, picking a Kith from the big list really isn't that hard. You should be able to skim and narrow it down to a most six without much fuss. I think the problem comes more from if you're looking to Kiths to inspire your character, because then it's harder to just narrow it down to the ones that fit what you already had in mind.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there's a practical way to group them. At least not in the text. Once the book is out, it shouldn't be that hard to plop them into a spreadsheet or something that allows for you to organize them interactively by assorting them according to different groupings to find a cluster that you're looking for more quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:58:59-07:00","id":557226,"title":"","content":"Although I love the changes in Changeling, I understand the concerns about the amount of kiths. It can be a drawback, specially for new players of gamemasters. I think they should be grouped in some tematical way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T18:44:56-07:00","id":557688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555632#post555632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My friend was interested in Changeling.<br /> <br /> Now he is not.<br /> <br /> His reason? He <i>has</i> to pick a Kith... out of a list of about 100.<br /> <br /> He <i>hates</i> having to pick one option off a long list - at least in 1e he had the choice of not picking a Kith, and the Kiths were in lists of about 20.<br /> <br /> That's my issue with the shift in focus; Kiths are so much more important now, so you can't really avoid interacting with THE LIST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a plan for this. For whatever that's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T18:52:25-07:00","id":557723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=557688#post557688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got a plan for this. For whatever that's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice to hear; I've been trying to get him to play more NWoD, and the dude's a bit finicky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:14:23-07:00","id":560269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalvin8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555325#post555325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. My own Fairest is calloused and cold. His escape had nothing to do with any kind of sense of personal responsibility. I'm open to re-contextualizing the character. But I want it to be on my terms. Not in adherence to push a Seeming into defacto leadership.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character might not be &quot;Fairest&quot; in Second Edition. You can apply the appropriate &quot;Pretty Person&quot; Kith, with a Seeming that fits the character's themes under the new definition of Seeming. That's what I had to do with my concept for Julie D'Aubigny as a Changeling for &quot;Lily, Sabre, Thorn&quot;. For First Edition she's a Fairest Dancer, but Second Edition wise she'll probably be a Beast Dancer (because she's all about flaunting social convention). And just stock up on Vainglorious Contract Clauses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:42:51-07:00","id":560510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=557688#post557688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got a plan for this. For whatever that's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to do this would be to divide the kiths into Mental, Social and Physical kiths. Not really giving them any other mechanical changes but rather just to show a player &quot;You want to make a Sherlock character? Then these are the kiths you want to have. You want to make a fighting character? Consider these kiths.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T19:27:21-07:00","id":562507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=560510#post560510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One way to do this would be to divide the kiths into Mental, Social and Physical kiths. Not really giving them any other mechanical changes but rather just to show a player &quot;You want to make a Sherlock character? Then these are the kiths you want to have. You want to make a fighting character? Consider these kiths.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not too far off what we're going with here. We have one more basic method of narrowing them down, so if you want, you can have a player picking from about 3-12 Kiths, instead of the whole list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T19:46:53-07:00","id":562516,"title":"","content":"People unhappy with too many options. That is a new one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:40:37-07:00","id":562550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562516#post562516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People unhappy with too many options. That is a new one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I can totally see choice paralysis as being a thing. In Requiem, you just pick one of five things. That's easy. But going through a list of 100 things can be a chore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:49:50-07:00","id":562565,"title":"","content":"Seriously. A lot of them are updated versions of old kiths, which I have sort of stored in my head neatly, and I thought removing Seeming wasn't going to slow me down at all.<br /> <br /> The preview made me pause once I realized how many pages I had already gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T23:24:14-07:00","id":562693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555283#post555283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly just adding the new direction for Seemings to the list of reasons why I'm really not excited for 2e. The game as a whole appears to be headed in a direction that I really don't care for, and has lost the magic of the original.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eleusis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555287#post555287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the method of escape giving you the Seeming, but in that case tying them to physical appearances seems odd to me.<br /> <br /> I also really do not like the new direction of the Fairest, which were my favorite 1E splat because of their fey callousness, whereas now their whole thing is feeling responsibility more than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalvin8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=555325#post555325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one friend who plays a Trickster Fox Changeling. A Beast seeming. For this player the novelty of the character includes the thematic of the Beast Seeming, which for her has been the largest descriptor of her character for three years now.<br /> The Character is highly social, as befitting a sly trickster and suave manipulator. But 2e Beast overtly contextualizes the seeming as anti-social, even anti-culture. She is presently frustrated with how to re-frame her own character to this new design. The Cruse and Blessing mechanics directly conflict with the character's design. I should further state she is very open to changing this character's Seeming. But for her the new Beast design/sample/example rubs her raw.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest here. If I can't get the players that sit at my table excited about 2e Changeling. I have no use for it. This thread is my attempt to make my concerns known. I hope it is coming across respectfully. I love a lot of the rest that is coming with this new edition of Changeling. But for five out of seven of my friends, these samples alone have turned them cold to even broaching the topic of a 2e game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must echo all of these posts in the dissatisfaction those I play with and I are feeling with the previewed information we've read regarding Changeling 2e. While I like the idea of switching Kiths and Seemings in theory, since many players just took Dual Kith anyway, much of the additional changes to the fluff surrounding this innocuous alteration seem entirely unasked for and do absolutely nothing but disrupt the original flavor of the game and limit choices we previously had. In presenting Kiths and Seemings in this new way, a specific sort of narrative is being forced on the player, one that goes against the very broad approach that the original game had.<br /> <br /> When you say you're going to switch Kiths and Seemings to just do what everyone did anyway, that's really a savvy observation of the fanbase's behavior and all you need to do. Otherwise, Changeling was already good and Changeling's players were already satisfied with how it was. You don't need to fix what isn't broken, and the more you alter something from its original portrayal, even in fine details, the more it stops being what it used to be. Such fine details are things like privateers and Loyalists no longer getting to be actual Changelings for no good reason, which damages their significance as antagonists in subtle but absolutely significant ways.<br /> <br /> Ideally, Changeling's fluff should have been largely preserved, taking the original corebook as a foundation and drawing from its proceeding sourcebooks with regards to how they expounded upon various details and further unified the gameline as a whole. When I read that things were being altered to fit &quot;in line&quot; with nWoD 2e stylistically, I could only look from side to side and then pensively ask, &quot;Why?&quot; Changeling was already pretty grimdark in and of itself and, as is par for the course, took the myths and legends of old and applied them to a modern context. Given that, in what way does it not already stylistically fit what we've come to know as the World of Darkness? Bringing it further &quot;in line&quot; with any sort of unified style only serves to make it lose its unique fairytale aesthetic, something that I <i>definitely</i> felt was missing from every single preview.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that's something of a theme a friend of mine has been seeing with nWoD 2e products: too much focus on style and flash. Everyone is dangerous and sexy and primal; the vampires are dangerous and sexy and primal; the werewolves are dangerous and sexy and primal; and every sort of Changeling Seeming is their own brand of dangerous and sexy and primal. In approaching the fluff this way, much of the substance and meaning behind each splat has slowly begun to slip away and they're all beginning to read the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1857-nahash","name":"Nahash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T00:10:46-07:00","id":562719,"title":"","content":"I never get why people take the, &quot;if it isn't broken, don't fix it,&quot; mentality to shut down the possibility of making something better. If you end up liking CtL 1e better, it exists and is fully playable. That is no reason to reject the idea that the people working on the games shouldn't try to make a better game; even if that better game ends up not appealing to everyone.<br /> <br /> The idea that CtL 1e doesn't have lots of places for improvement... just doesn't hold up to scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Frankly, critiques like this are the bane of open development. They are truly flash with no substance. A lot of generalities, buzzwords, and nothing to actually offer the developers something to really think about; the idea the some people don't like change is something they knew well ahead of time.<br /> <br /> Nothing demonstrates this better than the last point. Anyone that can read Demon, VtR 2e, WtF 2e, and Beast (all the 2e lines we have enough information to make full judgements on in this regard), and call them &quot;samey,&quot; sounds like someone that hasn't really read what's in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T17:27:38-07:00","id":563571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nahash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562693#post562693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must echo all of these posts in the dissatisfaction those I play with and I are feeling with the previewed information we've read regarding Changeling 2e. While I like the idea of switching Kiths and Seemings in theory, since many players just took Dual Kith anyway, much of the additional changes to the fluff surrounding this innocuous alteration seem entirely unasked for and do absolutely nothing but disrupt the original flavor of the game and limit choices we previously had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't conflate &quot;I didn't ask for it&quot; with &quot;it was unasked for.&quot; For one. <br /> <br /> For another, I'm sorry you feel that your choices are limited. However, I've had no small number of comments to the contrary, saying that they felt limited before, but now they feel more free to try new combinations of things previously unavailable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nahash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562693#post562693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say you're going to switch Kiths and Seemings to just do what everyone did anyway, that's really a savvy observation of the fanbase's behavior and all you need to do. Otherwise, Changeling was already good and Changeling's players were already satisfied with how it was. You don't need to fix what isn't broken, and the more you alter something from its original portrayal, even in fine details, the more it stops being what it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want me to not act on lessons learned over ten years of playing the game, and make shifts to emphasize play styles, themes, and moods I feel are important to the game, that's certainly an opinion. But as an artist, I have very little interest in spending a year out of my life simply rehashing and repeating someone else's work. To me, that's boring, derivative, and absolutely not a fulfilling practice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nahash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562693#post562693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such fine details are things like privateers and Loyalists no longer getting to be actual Changelings for no good reason, which damages their significance as antagonists in subtle but absolutely significant ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is a sticking point for you, a real sticking point, I'd like you to point out for me where that's been announced. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nahash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562693#post562693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally, Changeling's fluff should have been largely preserved, taking the original corebook as a foundation and drawing from its proceeding sourcebooks with regards to how they expounded upon various details and further unified the gameline as a whole. When I read that things were being altered to fit &quot;in line&quot; with nWoD 2e stylistically, I could only look from side to side and then pensively ask, &quot;Why?&quot; Changeling was already pretty grimdark in and of itself and, as is par for the course, took the myths and legends of old and applied them to a modern context. Given that, in what way does it not already stylistically fit what we've come to know as the World of Darkness? Bringing it further &quot;in line&quot; with any sort of unified style only serves to make it lose its unique fairytale aesthetic, something that I <i>definitely</i> felt was missing from every single preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you so <i>definitely</i> felt that. Ironically, one thing that came up frequently in discussion with my team was, we felt 1e was missing that. That while it had options to look like things, it had very few meaningful ties to what characters <i>actually do</i>. The expected play loop had absolutely nothing to do with a fairytale aesthetic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nahash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562693#post562693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, that's something of a theme a friend of mine has been seeing with nWoD 2e products: too much focus on style and flash. Everyone is dangerous and sexy and primal; the vampires are dangerous and sexy and primal; the werewolves are dangerous and sexy and primal; and every sort of Changeling Seeming is their own brand of dangerous and sexy and primal. In approaching the fluff this way, much of the substance and meaning behind each splat has slowly begun to slip away and they're all beginning to read the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're getting that reading, I'm not sure I can change your mind. Fortunately, if you're not interested in the direction of Second Edition, you have first edition books to draw from. Your opposition doesn't seem to be to Changeling 2e, insomuch as you oppose a very specific, very narrow, very reductionist read of Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T17:29:02-07:00","id":563573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562719#post562719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never get why people take the, &quot;if it isn't broken, don't fix it,&quot; mentality to shut down the possibility of making something better. If you end up liking CtL 1e better, it exists and is fully playable. That is no reason to reject the idea that the people working on the games shouldn't try to make a better game; even if that better game ends up not appealing to everyone.<br /> <br /> The idea that CtL 1e doesn't have lots of places for improvement... just doesn't hold up to scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Frankly, critiques like this are the bane of open development. They are truly flash with no substance. A lot of generalities, buzzwords, and nothing to actually offer the developers something to really think about; the idea the some people don't like change is something they knew well ahead of time.<br /> <br /> Nothing demonstrates this better than the last point. Anyone that can read Demon, VtR 2e, WtF 2e, and Beast (all the 2e lines we have enough information to make full judgements on in this regard), and call them &quot;samey,&quot; sounds like someone that hasn't really read what's in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went to all the trouble of an extended reply before reading this. This more or less covers it. <br /> <br /> &quot;Don't change anything!&quot; is literally the worst thing you can tell a developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:04:40-07:00","id":563630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=562719#post562719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never get why people take the, &quot;if it isn't broken, don't fix it,&quot; mentality to shut down the possibility of making something better. If you end up liking CtL 1e better, it exists and is fully playable. That is no reason to reject the idea that the people working on the games shouldn't try to make a better game; even if that better game ends up not appealing to everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're throwing out the baby with the bathwater. If Changelings are defined by their archetype, and don't have the opportunity of growing or expressing their characterization beyond that archetype, are they still Changelings anymore? Should the game still be tied in with a familiar brand name?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:41:06-07:00","id":563661,"title":"","content":"You need to be more specific to have a point.<br /> <br /> When the nWOD came out, people were saying that the baby was being thrown out, and the nWOD shouldn't be called a &quot;WOD&quot; and the game lines all got the same sort of treatment. Requiem isn't Masquerade. It threw out the baby and doesn't deserve to be called Vampire any more. Discussions of the WOD have seen this about the nWOD, and every nWOD game line that shares a name with a cWOD one. It's happened in all of the nWOD 1e to 2e transitions.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every WOD splat ever is partially defined by archetypes, because archetypes are the basis of splats. Ventrue are the noble vampires, Gangrel are beastial ones. Full Moon werewolves are warriors and Crescent Moon ones are spirit workers.<br /> <br /> 1e Changelings at Seemings, Kiths, and Courts, that define a character through archetypes. 2e does too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:43:07-07:00","id":563692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=563630#post563630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are defined by their archetype, and don't have the opportunity of growing or expressing their characterization beyond that archetype</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point out anywhere that this has been even remotely suggested?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T07:38:39-07:00","id":564126,"title":"","content":"I agree. I -like- where things are going. But the more I see of the various seemings the more limiting they are starting to feel. My main benchmark being that many of my favorite characters (Both my own and others) from the past edition don't even seem possible to make. The way Ogres are now heartless sorts, or Darklings betrayed, or whatever. Crazily, one of my own Darklings would now be a Fairest if I kept the story exactly the same!<br /> <br /> STill not enough for me to be sold off it, as the whole package could easily change things. But at a glance they do seem a lot more limiting.<br /> <br /> Flipside being, I ADORE the new way Kiths are handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T08:20:28-07:00","id":564140,"title":"","content":"As has been stated already, most of these complaints are for things that do not seem to be present in the teasers. Changeling has always been a game that, for me at least, inspired a great deal of creative lateral thinking and after reading these forums for some time I do not think I am alone. The people complaining appear to have taken the opposite view though and have boxed the game in with either a very narrow perception of what the game is and can be or seek (strangely) a reduction of options, as seen with those who are complaining about the plethora of options being offered through the greatly expanded kith list. To take a specific example that someone mentioned regarding the unsuitability of the Beast Seeming for their player's Fox/Trickster character, then don't use Beast with that character. We are going to have not only a massive kith list (which it baffles me why this is seen as a negative) but additional Seemings as well. It is easier than ever now to find combinations that suit a character's personality and ambitions. The information we have so far makes it look like we will have more freedom to create in the new edition which seems pretty appropriate for the Changeling setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T08:35:59-07:00","id":564151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564140#post564140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been stated already, most of these complaints are for things that do not seem to be present in the teasers. Changeling has always been a game that, for me at least, inspired a great deal of creative lateral thinking and after reading these forums for some time I do not think I am alone. The people complaining appear to have taken the opposite view though and have boxed the game in with either a very narrow perception of what the game is and can be or seek (strangely) a reduction of options, as seen with those who are complaining about the plethora of options being offered through the greatly expanded kith list. To take a specific example that someone mentioned regarding the unsuitability of the Beast Seeming for their player's Fox/Trickster character, then don't use Beast with that character. We are going to have not only a massive kith list (which it baffles me why this is seen as a negative) but additional Seemings as well. It is easier than ever now to find combinations that suit a character's personality and ambitions. The information we have so far makes it look like we will have more freedom to create in the new edition which seems pretty appropriate for the Changeling setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, more of this please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:00:14-07:00","id":564321,"title":"","content":"I concur. My concerns is that the Seeming presentation hides the flexibility and diversity of the new options. I never felt or said that they lack flexibility or are a step backwards.<br /> <br /> (I did kinda feel that the deemphasis on the Seasonal courts weakened the abuse survivor metaphor but MachineIV convinced me otherwise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:45:54-07:00","id":564450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564140#post564140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We are going to have not only a massive kith list (which it baffles me why this is seen as a negative)</div> </div> </div> </div> Decision paralysis. Too many options can feel overwhelming for people, which is a real problem. Too much of a good thing, and all. <br /> <br /> Personally, I feel like we're still missing the key to bring the whole Court and Seeming stuff in sharp focus. The Contracts. Without seeing them, I feel like I'm missing a chunk of understanding here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:51:57-07:00","id":564514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564450#post564450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Decision paralysis. Too many options can feel overwhelming for people, which is a real problem. Too much of a good thing, and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This much is true. That said, while this is a genuine concern, the negatives to it can be counter-balanced to some degree by way of execution. Notions like the one Dave mentioned to help narrow things down are good moves. If instead of picking from ~100 options, you can choose to pick from a number of groups (and perhaps sub-groups) denoting ballparks of interest, that can become a lot less daunting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I feel like we're still missing the key to bring the whole Court and Seeming stuff in sharp focus. The Contracts. Without seeing them, I feel like I'm missing a chunk of understanding here. </div> </div> </div>There is probably no part of Changeling 2e I <i>don't</i> want to see a post about, but I agree that this one is certainly up there, regarding context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:11:43-07:00","id":564640,"title":"","content":"You're not missing anything with the contracts. It's window dressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:48:36-07:00","id":564664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564640#post564640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not missing anything with the contracts. It's window dressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there could always be a surprise in the presentation and execution of them that we haven't heard about yet. But I suspect you're right.<br /> <br /> I admit my expression of interest was less from assistance in working out how the game's thematics work together, and more a desire to see how the mechanics work, and what cool things the team's put together. I mean, I guess seeing some of the Seeming-specific Clauses* on a Contract or two could help anyone for whom they haven't quite clicked? Mostly, it's just an interest in cool powers for characters to use.<br /> <br /> * Yep, still calling 'em that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:54:15-07:00","id":564788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564640#post564640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not missing anything with the contracts. It's window dressing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Affinity abilites are another avenue to explore understanding the Courts and Seemings. Its what I do for all the games to help me wrap my head around some things. So, no, its not window dressing for me. Its a critical aspect in understanding the splats, as well as methods to subvert and tweak characters.<br /> <br /> As well, for the Court Creation process? If creating affinity powers are going to be too large, I'm going to simply throw out the entire court creation step and only use whatever ones we already have. I'm not particularly interested in creating new powers for the games for each court system. There's a lot going on here where I want to see the mechanics behind it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:25:42-07:00","id":564924,"title":"","content":"After the most recent Court preview, the whole direction of Second Edition has really clicked for me - Second Edition is putting the spotlight on seizing the narrative of your life back from the Gentry, hence how each Court system reflects the narrative of that community, rather than a universal model applying. At first I was worried about taking the focus off the 4 Seasonal Courts would decrease the &quot;surviving trauma&quot; themes of the game (given that those 4 courts correspond intentionally to Denial (Spring), Anger (Summer), Bargaining (Autumn), and Depression (Winter)) but now I'm really seeing how they're taking it in a more intentionally empowering direction.<br /> <br /> Seeming reflecting the escape you seized for yourself, rather than what the Gentry turned you into (which is still there with Kith), is in the same model of the game increasing focus on that empowering theme.<br /> <br /> Do we know if Talecrafting is making it into the core? Possibly via the Pledge system? I would be very much on theme if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-23-2015, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:30:37-07:00","id":564925,"title":"","content":"Talecrafting is mentioned as one of the Court Affinity Contracts, isn't it? Or am I misremembering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:43:18-07:00","id":564941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564788#post564788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Affinity abilites are another avenue to explore understanding the Courts and Seemings. Its what I do for all the games to help me wrap my head around some things. So, no, its not window dressing for me. Its a critical aspect in understanding the splats, as well as methods to subvert and tweak characters.<br /> <br /> As well, for the Court Creation process? If creating affinity powers are going to be too large, I'm going to simply throw out the entire court creation step and only use whatever ones we already have. I'm not particularly interested in creating new powers for the games for each court system. There's a lot going on here where I want to see the mechanics behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I can put it simply.<br /> <br /> If you're having problems with the Court Creation system this far in, Contracts aren't going to change a damn thing, because the powers emphasizing aspects of the courts will only emphasize the problems perceived. Finding the right lighting for a statue you hate might make it tolerable, but it's not going to change the statue.<br /> <br /> If you're at least open-mined to the Court Creation system being something with potential, then yes, Contracts can be a deal maker or a deal break, because their emphasis <i>is</i> the thing that will tip the scales.The lighting will matter.<br /> <br /> But if a person isn't open-minded towards the Court Creation system, then I have very little reason to believe that person won't try it at least once regardless of Contracts, and how their gameplay experience with the system will determine their likelihood of supporting it far more than any amount of on-forum discussion will.<br /> <br /> So, I'm sorry if you think contracts aren't window dressing when they come to the Courts. They are potent and powerful plot twists players can use, and are important, but they matter a lot more to to the overall experience than the more particular experience of Courts. When it comes to the Courts, they are window dressing.<br /> <br /> This thing, that we have, that we're talking about? That is the meat of this corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-22-2015, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T23:24:54-07:00","id":565054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You need to be more specific to have a point.<br /> <br /> When the nWOD came out, people were saying that the baby was being thrown out, and the nWOD shouldn't be called a &quot;WOD&quot; and the game lines all got the same sort of treatment. Requiem isn't Masquerade. It threw out the baby and doesn't deserve to be called Vampire any more. Discussions of the WOD have seen this about the nWOD, and every nWOD game line that shares a name with a cWOD one. It's happened in all of the nWOD 1e to 2e transitions.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every WOD splat ever is partially defined by archetypes, because archetypes are the basis of splats. Ventrue are the noble vampires, Gangrel are beastial ones. Full Moon werewolves are warriors and Crescent Moon ones are spirit workers.<br /> <br /> 1e Changelings at Seemings, Kiths, and Courts, that define a character through archetypes. 2e does too. </div> </div> </div>I completely agree here. With 2E each Seeming is presenting an Archetype that helps contextualize what the Character HAS done and what they are PRONE to do in the future. My critiques were made without much context as what the intention was behind the sample write-ups in the context of the whole Book. I'll explain that short sightedness latter here.<br /> <br /> I have battled many a player over al problem that stems from the existence of Archetypes. Now I'll repeat what I just said above to keep from being confused. I fully support Archetypes as building blocks for Character design.<br /> I have told a couple players to check themselves when they are too stuck in a mindset of Stereotypes. (You\u2019re playing a Winter, fellow player. Act sadder. You\u2019re not playing that right.) That bullshit pisses me off.<br /> For further personal context. I hate the DnD class system. Even in a Fantasy Setting that could potentially promote a Caste System for Adventurers (Pathfinder). The Class System is little more than short-hand for what a Character is training to do in the effort to reach their goals. Most DnD players seem to take this system as a holy gospel. (You are playing a Cleric. Get behind the party.)<br /> <br /> I guess another way to contextualize MY original fear of the new Seeming Archetypes is that that the first three revealed read like Classes. I'll now explain my apparent confusion (ignorance?) of the intent behind the write-ups below.<br /> For example: We do have Orders, Tribes, and Covenants that seem to assume their own superiority. But they do so from a position of that being their stated goal as an organization. Seemings are instead personal representations of an internal choice. The Fairest Changeling made a choice to assume authority by taking responsibility. Leaders generally are responsible. But not every responsible person is a leader. Is this their Soul trying to force the Fairest into being a Leader after they exulted personal responsibility? Where does Seeming come from? Is it Wyrd enforcing a Narrative ON the Changeling?<br /> I thought it was the Changeling\u2019s Soul redefining their place in a Narrative being spun upon them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564140#post564140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been stated already, most of these complaints are for things that do not seem to be present in the teasers. Changeling has always been a game that, for me at least, inspired a great deal of creative lateral thinking and after reading these forums for some time I do not think I am alone. The people complaining appear to have taken the opposite view though and have boxed the game in with either a very narrow perception of what the game is and can be or seek (strangely) a reduction of options, as seen with those who are complaining about the plethora of options being offered through the greatly expanded kith list. To take a specific example that someone mentioned regarding the unsuitability of the Beast Seeming for their player's Fox/Trickster character, then don't use Beast with that character. We are going to have not only a massive kith list (which it baffles me why this is seen as a negative) but additional Seemings as well. It is easier than ever now to find combinations that suit a character's personality and ambitions. The information we have so far makes it look like we will have more freedom to create in the new edition which seems pretty appropriate for the Changeling setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget where I saw it, but it makes sense. The write-ups are intended to represent the most fanatically \u2018X\u2019 of a particular Seeming. With this understanding I can go to my players whining about the Darkling and say. <i>&quot;Sure, that is indeed what a fanatically \u2018Darkling\u2019 character would be. But your character is more than her Seeming. She has a Kith and in the future will ponder an association with a Court. She will have &quot;Vice&quot; and &quot;Virtue&quot; that will pin down her world view. And all of this is affects your Character's whole in whatever balance you like&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I still don\u2019t like that the Fairest revolve Around LEADERSHIP. I personally read from the first paragraphs that they seem more empowered by PERSONAL POTENTIAL. Or lack thereof. That might be a leadership trait, but so is fearlessness against insurmountable odds (Ogre) The willingness to take dangerous risks (Darkling) and the abandoning of traditional expectations (Beast) I like the direction of the Seeming Archetypes. I don't feel the execution of those Archetypes is perfect mechanically and fluff-wise. Accept Ogres. Ogres are almost on the nose as far as perfection goes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","user":"Khalvin8","date":". 06-23-2015, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T05:50:51-07:00","id":565271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=564941#post564941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me see if I can put it simply.</div> </div> </div> </div> i think you missed my point. I want to see the Contracts because I want to see how much work is involved here. Its not like I have copus amounts of free time to design stuff. That is a sticking point for me and my group. <br /> <br /> If you can't see how that might be important to some, then we have nothing to discuss. The Court Creation System (TM) has potential, but I have neither the time nor the inclination to use it if it'll require extensive effort in practice. <br /> <br /> The support for custom stuff is great... If you have the time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T08:34:35-07:00","id":566447,"title":"","content":"Oh, that.<br /> <br /> You're right, I missed that point by a mile.<br /> <br /> Still, imagine it's up to players. The breakdown of categories and application of Seemings to contracts points at contracts being a higher price, and in-house contracts being a court thing. If that's probable, then it's likely that some groups just decide on which contracts they want at price and run with that.<br /> <br /> But yeah, now I see the problem. Still not a big seller for me, but I see how it contributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:12:25-07:00","id":566551,"title":"","content":"Yes, that. Its actually a pretty important consideration in the gaming industry now, to the point where its actually D&amp;D's new business model - making it easier to sit down and play with the absolute minimum amount of work before hand. As the generation of gamers grow older, and more time is sucked up into work, family, and other avenues, less and less time can be devoted to hobbies. Everything is being designed with an eye towards making the effort outside the game as low as possible. <br /> <br /> Its actually a concern for me going forwards. Simply finding the time to hammer out Interlocks in Demon is an annoyance at times. This? Potentially much worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:20:37-07:00","id":566716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=566551#post566551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that. Its actually a pretty important consideration in the gaming industry now, to the point where its actually D&amp;D's new business model - making it easier to sit down and play with the absolute minimum amount of work before hand. As the generation of gamers grow older, and more time is sucked up into work, family, and other avenues, less and less time can be devoted to hobbies. Everything is being designed with an eye towards making the effort outside the game as low as possible.<br /> <br /> Its actually a concern for me going forwards. Simply finding the time to hammer out Interlocks in Demon is an annoyance at times. This? Potentially much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that-in fact, I had some problems with hammering out Interlocks, although I feel like that was personal time management. Writing for the Rose Courts has taken away from video editing, and yeah, that's been a problem.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Court Creation is supposed to be session zero, so the time you usually cut out for gaming can serve as the building. But adding in Contracts is a bit of a bother.<br /> <br /> I imagine the grand goal is to allow for either, though. Some groups have more time and enjoy that intimacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:44:25-07:00","id":566818,"title":"","content":"I like brewing up that kind of stuff because for me it's often the closest I get to actually playing. I think Changeling is going in a great direction with Courts because by the look of things you'll easily be able to just pick up and play with the sample courts if that suits your group's needs, but there are also options to custom-make new ones if that's what you enjoy doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:00:01-07:00","id":566900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=566818#post566818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like brewing up that kind of stuff because for me it's often the closest I get to actually playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello, kindred spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Changeling is going in a great direction with Courts because by the look of things you'll easily be able to just pick up and play with the sample courts if that suits your group's needs, but there are also options to custom-make new ones if that's what you enjoy doing. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I also feel that guidelines like this reduce the difficulty for homebrewers. That's liable to increase the number (and quality) of fan-created Courts. Even if someone doesn't feel up to homebrewing a Court, that expands the options they have when browsing online; if it's not quite what they're after, it may be close enough to tweak from there easily enough. Never mind simply requesting some support from the community on the mechanics side of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:08:47-07:00","id":569215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=566551#post566551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that. Its actually a pretty important consideration in the gaming industry now, to the point where its actually D&amp;D's new business model - making it easier to sit down and play with the absolute minimum amount of work before hand. As the generation of gamers grow older, and more time is sucked up into work, family, and other avenues, less and less time can be devoted to hobbies. Everything is being designed with an eye towards making the effort outside the game as low as possible.<br /> <br /> Its actually a concern for me going forwards. Simply finding the time to hammer out Interlocks in Demon is an annoyance at times. This? Potentially much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking through the Court Creation Thread and considering the City examples currently in the works, I think you and other players will have a host of Sample Courts(and Contracts) you can lift directly into your game. Just because you do not have a lot of time to prepare doesn't mean there are no resources available to you that you can just use. The Great Courts will be represented in Core almost as they were in 1e.<br /> I understand your point about a ageing demographic and a general loss of available time for hobbies, but none of that seems relevant in the face of so much Fan and Source Material flying off keyboards as we speak.<br /> <br /> I know My own Courts of Mountain and River will work for nearly any Interior City as long as said City rest within 20 miles of a Mountain and on the banks of a River.<br /> You will have Seasonal and Seelie courts out of the box as well as the Toronto 1001 Nights Freehold. All of them easily ported into any city anywhere.<br /> I've seen someone working to modify the Directional and Diurnal Courts into 2e as well. Those too are easily lifted into any geographic space you wish.<br /> Finally I would happily do some leg work for you if you have an idea of your own you just don't have time to develope.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to shut you down here. Understand you have at least this forum at your disposal to help you build your Setting if your time is caught up in your work and family life and keeps you from having to many distraction around like writing up Contracts and Court Themes. Other nerds with more free time would be happy to help enable your Campaign. I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:14:00-07:00","id":569571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/553801-my-issues-with-the-new-direction-with-seemings?p=566551#post566551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that. Its actually a pretty important consideration in the gaming industry now, to the point where its actually D&amp;D's new business model - making it easier to sit down and play with the absolute minimum amount of work before hand. As the generation of gamers grow older, and more time is sucked up into work, family, and other avenues, less and less time can be devoted to hobbies. Everything is being designed with an eye towards making the effort outside the game as low as possible.<br /> <br /> Its actually a concern for me going forwards. Simply finding the time to hammer out Interlocks in Demon is an annoyance at times. This? Potentially much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not entirely sure how true this is for most dungeon masters or storytellers or what have you. The old school renaissance, which appears to have been widespread enough to have had a significant impact on the new direction D&amp;D has taken, was fueled as much by a renewed interest in sandbox-style games and megadungeons, which create a lot of work for the game master, as it was by an appreciation for Gygax-era adventure modules. Most of the game masters I know are constantly tinkering with systems and settings; even when they run published adventures, they tend to spend a fair amount of time modifying things to their liking.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you're wrong; obviously you're speaking from personal experience. However, I think that the Court Creation system will be useful to a lot of gamers who like to build things from scratch anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:26:27-07:00","id":569601,"title":"","content":"At least in the case of 5th edition, you're both right. Their biggest design goal was to create a simple, streamlined skeleton that can just be picked up and played with very easily, but is friendly to tinkering and has a lot of built-in options for adding layers of complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:01:17-07:00","id":570466,"title":"","content":"it is fun to see this game evolve before our eyes. i appreciate the deep thought and design considerations that have been put into this addition by the creative team.<br /> <br /> personally, i am going to stick with 1e changeling: the lost. i really enjoy it. as does my group. it is good medium crunch game, with enough open space to get really inventive. also, as has been mentioned above by another forumite... we are all super busy adults that have become casual gamers by necessity because real life. the amount of player investment during the character creation mini-game is pretty substantial. <br /> <br /> i do not feel that this new editions sucks, or that the developer should have stayed true to the first edition. 1e was pretty great. solid. you couldn't really improve on it. why not make a new game that expands on things hinted upon in the old one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:37:12-07:00","id":570898,"title":"","content":"To each his own. From what I've seen, the changes in the new edition are going to bring more nuance to the game, and I much prefer the second edition nWoD rules to the first. If nothing else, I'll be glad to have updated contracts and the like.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I can sympathize with wanting a game that's simple to pick up and play, but World of Darkness has never struck me as particularly casual. I don't mean that in a &quot;go play something else, noob&quot; kind of way; most of my WoD games, old or new, have crashed and burned after not too terribly long. I'd be hard pressed to think of another major game system that takes as much work and player buy-in to get right. But I really like world building, and I've had a lot of fun playing with the Court Building system and playing with character concepts mixing and matching Seemings and Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}